    "DialogText": "The Silmarils were lost to the world after the fall of Morgoth. One is bound within the sea, another is carried among the stars, and the third… It was taken by the one who would not relinquish it, Maedhros, son of Fëanor. Legend holds that Maedhros cast himself and the Silmaril into a fiery chasm in the depths of the earth. Yet, such a jewel cannot remain lost forever. Perhaps it has surfaced once more, drawn up by the labor of Dwarves, who dig deep and uncover what others cannot.

